sequenceDiagram
    participant P as Producer agent (org A)
    participant W as WireProtocol (LF A2A default, D-IMPL-14)
    participant CCP as Consumer Control Plane
    participant L2 as Consumer L2 Assembly (only writer)
    participant L3 as Consumer L3 Graph

    P->>P: Sign product (detached JWS over canonical serialization, D-IMPL-15)
    P->>W: Emit typed Context Product (artifact payload)
    W->>CCP: Deliver inbound product (mTLS transport identity)
    CCP->>CCP: Verify signature (producer identity, version, key id)
    CCP->>CCP: Verify Policy bindings + contract validation + lineage integrity (D-IMPL-16, every product, no fast path)
    alt Verification passes
        CCP->>L2: Admit product for assembly
        L2->>L3: Write with lineage set-union (inbound L extends consumer L - producer plan, snapshot, policy version preserved)
    else Verification fails
        CCP->>CCP: Reject admission - audited rejection record, product never reaches L3
        CCP-->>W: Rejection response to producer
    end
